+### [Parallel Marching Cubes](12211-parallel-marching-cubes.md)
+Parallel Marching Cubes is a parallel implementation of the Marching Cubes algorithm designed to compute isosurfaces of huge datasets that cannot fit entirely into a single machine's memory. It solves the memory bottleneck of traditional sequential Marching Cubes by using a piecewise slice strategy along the k-direction, requiring only that at least two slices fit into physical memory. Unlike siblings that assume the entire volume fits in RAM, this method distributes the workload across multiple processes or threads, enabling the processing of datasets with millions of grid values on multi-processor architectures.
 
